 OS confinement.","guidance":"Use a fresh context independent of author history. Inspect the exact candidate read-only; report criteria violations, not repair procedures. No execution authority is granted.","criteria":[]},"Head":"bd2af87f244b4c63b640efa29e893dfc2de5ddc1","Intent":"feat(review): run Greenhouse in parallel with built-in review per Project and compare Verdicts (Phase 1 G-3)\n\nDone when: A Project config key `review_parallel = \"greenhouse\"` (unset by default) makes Posse request a Greenhouse Verdict through the G-2 adapter for each head the built-in loop reviews, and record it in the G-1 Verdict table with `mode = parallel`, as specified in docs/research/2026-11-13-direction-2-design.md sections 2.6 and 2.8 (step G-3).; A Project with the key set and no built-in review (`defaults.review = none`) still gets a parallel Verdict for each PR head it gates. Those rows count toward reliability, inconclusive share, wrong-head and latency, and never toward recall.; Parallel Verdicts and their findings are stored only. They never reach the author, never block or allow Publish or Merge, and a Greenhouse failure or refusal never delays the built-in loop. A failure raises at most one Notice per head.; `posse stats` gains a review comparison that computes every G1 threshold in section 2.6 from stored rows, per Project and in total, with the number of reviewed heads.; The key is frozen in each admitted Task's plan. Unsetting it stops new parallel requests and changes nothing else.; No change to existing review, publish or merge behaviour when the key is unset.","Paths":["docs/research/2026-11-13-direction-2-design.md","docs/spec.md","internal/app/greenhouse.go","internal/app/project_remove_test.go","internal/app/review_comparison.go","internal/app/review_comparison_test.go","internal/app/review_rounds.go","internal/app/stats.go","internal/app/task_plan.go","internal/config/config.go","internal/config/config_test.go","internal/config/schema.go","internal/e2e/profile